<!--CLI Documentation — Introduction
  FQN: com.machineblocks.bml.cli.documentation.Introduction-->
<clidoc:Introduction xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.bml.core"
  xmlns:clidoc="com.machineblocks.bml.cli.documentation">

  <baseType>
    core:Documentation
  </baseType>
  <is>
    Purpose of the MachineBlocks host CLI
  </is>
  <documentation>
    MachineBlocks users want BML turned into OpenSCAD that matches the V3 SCAD
    library. They should not have to install the BlockML toolchain repository or
    learn every compiler target.

    This package is that simplified view:

    - It depends on published @blockml/* packages (universal CLI and compiler).
    - It depends on @machineblocks/render-target and therefore on
      @blockml/block-render-engine.
    - It depends on @machineblocks/core. The render target peers that package.
      init records it in the consumer project's dependencies, beside @blockml/core.
    - It registers registry name machineblocks-v3-scad.
    - It fills MachineBlocks defaults: where the SCAD library lives, where
      OpenSCAD is, where .scad files are written.

    The universal command remains blockml from @blockml/cli. That command must
    not hardcode MachineBlocks. Product UX for this domain is this package.

    Analogy: tsc is the language tool; a product CLI can wrap it. MachineBlocks
    users install this CLI. They do not clone blockml.

    V1 of this library is the contract. The bin follows these blocks.

  </documentation>
  <references>
    <see type="clidoc:DualCliModel" relation="ReadNext" />
  </references>
</clidoc:Introduction>
